{"availability":"available","full":"Avnsx/win11_release_guard","name":"win11_release_guard","description":"Easily compare the local devices windows release & build version, against broadly available official Windows 11 versioning. Detects silent updating-issues. This Repository also acts as the always up to date web-source of truth, it displays signed info accessible programmatically through designated GitHub pages.","category":"Design","language":"Python","stars":2,"forks":1,"created":"2026-05-28T16:33:12Z","updated":"2026-10-09T14:53:31Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://avnsx.github.io/win11_release_guard/","topics":["compliance","endpoint-management","github-actions","github-pages","json-api","microsoft-release-health","pypi","python","release-automation","release-monitoring","rmm","security-automation","sysadmin","trusted-publishing","win11","windows","windows-11","windows-admin","windows-update"],"demo":"https://avnsx.github.io/win11_release_guard/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T02:05:20.372Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T02:05:20.372Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T02:05:20.372Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T02:05:20.372Z","stars":2,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Windows release policy guard for broad-fleet Windows 11 version checks.","Windows 11 Release Guard tells administrators whether an existing Windows 11 device is on the current fleet release and quality baseline, using a signed JSON feed, build-first local evidence, a static GitHub Pages dashboard/API, and a PyPI package for sysadmin/RMM automation. The repository, distribution package, installed console command, and Python import package use the same win11releaseguard name.","Compliance trust comes from the signed public policy JSON plus detached signature, not from display labels or badge state. Start with Policy Feed and Trust Model and Local Windows Detection."],"features":[],"sourceUrl"